 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Out-of-Bounds Points:** Points falling outside `grid_range` are discarded via the mask [S3].
-*   **Capacity Limits:** If the number of unique voxels exceeds `max_num_voxels`, the loop breaks, leaving subsequent points unprocessed [S3].
-*   **Point Overflow:** If a voxel contains more than `max_points_in_voxel` points, only the first `max_points_in_voxel` are stored; subsequent points are discarded [S3].
-*   **Axis Convention:** The coordinate axis order is reversed (x,y,z $\to$ z,y,x) to align with the memory layout of `coor_to_voxelidx` [S3].
