 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** $O(N)$ for coordinate computation and masking, where $N$ is the number of points. The main loop is $O(V)$ where $V$ is the number of unique voxels, but bounded by $N$. Hashing via the dense `coor_to_voxelidx` array allows $O(1)$ lookup per point [S3].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** Dominated by the pre-allocated buffers `voxels` and `coor_to_voxelidx`. Memory usage is $O(max\_num\_voxels \times max\_points\_in\_voxel \times F + grid\_size[0] \times grid\_size[1] \times grid\_size[2])$ [S3].
-*   **Performance:** The Numba JIT version (`voxelize_jit`) significantly reduces Python overhead compared to the pure NumPy version (`voxelize`), making it suitable for real-time applications [S3].
-*   **Strengths:** Simple implementation, efficient for sparse point clouds, supports feature aggregation [S2, S3].
-*   **Limitations:** Fixed capacity limits require careful tuning; dense coordinate map can be memory-intensive for large grids with small voxel sizes [S3].
+*   **Time Complexity:** $O(N)$ for coordinate computation and masking, where $N$ is the number of points [S3, unofficial]. The main loop is $O(V)$ where $V$ is the number of unique voxels, but bounded by $N$ [S3, unofficial]. Hashing via the dense `coor_to_voxelidx` array allows $O(1)$ lookup per point [S3, unofficial].
+*   **Memory Complexity:** Dominated by the pre-allocated buffers `voxels` and `coor_to_voxelidx` [S3, unofficial]. Memory usage is $O(max\_num\_voxels \times max\_points\_in\_voxel \times F + grid\_size[0] \times grid\_size[1] \times grid\_size[2])$ [S3, unofficial].
+*   **Performance:** The Numba JIT version (`voxelize_jit`) significantly reduces Python overhead compared to the pure NumPy version (`voxelize`), making it suitable for real-time applications [S3, unofficial].
+*   **Strengths:** Simple implementation, efficient for sparse point clouds due to JIT compilation, supports feature aggregation [S2, S3, unofficial].
+*   **Limitations:** Fixed capacity limits require careful tuning; dense coordinate map can be memory-intensive for large grids with small voxel sizes [S3, unofficial].
