 ## Background
-Point cloud voxelization is a fundamental preprocessing step in 3D computer vision, particularly for LiDAR and depth-sensor data. Open3D provides a high-level API `create_from_point_cloud` which creates a voxel grid where occupied voxels store the average color of points within them [S2]. The specific sparse voxel grid implementation detailed here, including the JIT-optimized version, originates from repositories such as `danielhavir/voxelize3d` [S3].
+Point cloud voxelization creates a voxel grid from a point cloud where occupied voxels store aggregated point data [S2]. The sparse voxel grid implementation detailed here, including the JIT-optimized version, is provided by [S3, unofficial].
 
